# =============================================================================
# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# Root cause this file fixes: without it, `COPY ClinicNow.Worker/ ClinicNow.Worker/`
# (and the equivalent for every other project) sends this machine's own bin/obj/
# folders into the build context. Those folders contain restore artifacts
# (project.assets.json, *.nuget.g.props) with this HOST'S absolute paths baked in
# (e.g. a Windows NuGet fallback folder path) - copying them into a Linux build
# container overwrites the correct Linux-native restore output that
# `RUN dotnet restore` just produced inside the container, and `dotnet publish
# --no-restore` then fails trying to resolve packages via a path that doesn't
# exist in Linux. Same category of bug .gitignore already prevents for git;
# Docker needs its own, separate exclusion file.
# =============================================================================

# --- .NET build output - always regenerated inside the container ---
**/bin/
**/obj/
**/*.user
**/*.suo
**/.vs/

# --- Secrets - Dockerfiles never COPY .env; keep it out of the build context too ---
.env
.env.example
*.env

# --- Flutter/Dart UI - neither Dockerfile ever COPYs UI/, excluding it keeps the
# build context small (Flutter build/.dart_tool output can be large) ---
UI/

# --- VCS / tooling noise ---
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
*.md
